"url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/47482708/notre-dame-wr-jordan-faison-play-lacrosse-season","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Adam Rittenberg","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Notre Dame's Jordan Faison to miss 1-2 weeks with ankle injury","description":"Notre Dame starting wide receiver Jordan Faison suffered a sprained right ankle against Texas A&M and will miss one to two weeks.","published":"2024-09-03T01:37:46.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/41097668/notre-dame-jordan-faison-miss-1-2-weeks-ankle-injury","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Adam Rittenberg","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"College Football Playoff top 12 projection after Week 11","description":"We assess how the selection committee could stack the top teams in the country after Week 11.","published":"2026-11-15T13:13:29.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50480953/projecting-2026-playoff-top-12-week-11-cfp","type":"Story","byline":"Heather Dinich","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"No. 2 Utah survives, stays unbeaten on late 70-yard TD in thriller vs. Arizona","description":"In a back-and-forth thriller, Utah rallied to remain undefeated after Devon Dampier hit Creed Whittemore on a 70-yard score late in a 40-39 win over Arizona.","published":"2026-11-15T14:23:38.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50488650/no-2-utah-survives-late-70-yard-td-thriller-vs-arizona","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Patience starting to run thin for head coaches in Week 11","description":"Saturday didn't offer much to change the season's complexion, but some coaches are coming under pressure.","published":"2026-11-15T08:17:38.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/page/gamedayfinal111426/week-11-top-games-highlights-takeaways","type":"Story","byline":"Kyle Bonagura","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Predicting the College Football Playoff: Who's most likely to make the field?","description":"Find out which teams our experts think will make this season's CFP.","published":"2026-11-15T07:48:30.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/page/playoffpredictions111426/cfp-predictions-week-11","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN Staff","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Kiffin understands frustration as LSU's playoff hopes dashed","description":"LSU coach Lane Kiffin said it was fair to question the team's 6-4 record this season after losing to Texas on Saturday, a defeat that likely knocked LSU out of playoff contention.","published":"2026-11-15T08:55:17.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50488081/kiffin-understands-frustration-lsu-playoff-hopes-dashed","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Alex Scarborough","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Arch Manning leads game-winning drive as Texas stuns LSU","description":"Arch Manning found Raleek Brown for a 4-yard touchdown pass along the left sideline with 3 seconds left as Texas escaped Tiger Stadium with a victory over LSU","published":"2026-11-15T13:13:49.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50487515/arch-manning-leads-game-winning-drive-texas-stuns-lsu","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Wake Forest's post-blowout jab at SMU tops college football Week 11 trolls","description":"Wake Forest dominated SMU on the gridiron Saturday -- and added insult to injury after the game.","published":"2026-11-15T05:30:15.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50481104/college-football-trolls-week-11","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN staff","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Who are the winningest college football coaches of all time?","description":"From Saban to Paterno, there are many legendary college football coaches. Who has the best career record? Check out who has the most wins now.","published":"2026-11-15T04:25:09.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/39283806/who-winningest-college-football-coaches-all","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN","source":"ESPN"}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5150424/jordan-faison","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jordan_Faison"},"wiki":{"rules":4,"title":"Jordan Faison","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jordan_Faison","description":"American football and lacrosse player (born 2004)","touched":"2026-11-14T07:36:20Z","intro":"Quincy Jordan Faison II (born April 7, 2004) is an American college football wide receiver for the Notre Dame Fighting Irish. He previously also played midfielder for the Notre Dame Fighting Irish lacrosse team.","sections":[{"key":"early","title":"Early life","text":"Faison grew up in Weston, Florida and attended the Pine Crest School, where he played basketball, lacrosse, and football. In football, he played safety and quarterback in Pine Crest's Wing T offense and accumulated 1,800 all-purpose yards and scored 26 total touchdowns as a senior. Faison was a three-time All-American in lacrosse."},{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"Faison entered his freshman football season at Notre Dame as a walk-on before earning a football scholarship midway through the season. He was named the MVP of the 2023 Sun Bowl after catching five passes for 115 yards and a touchdown in a 48–8 win over Oregon State. Faison finished his freshman football season with 19 receptions for 322 yards and four touchdowns.\nFaison was a starting midfielder in his freshman season with the Notre Dame Fighting Irish men's lacrosse team and scored 22 goals. He scored a goal in Notre Dame's 15–5 victory in the 2024 National Championship game against Maryland. He retired from lacrosse in January 2026 to focus fully on football."}]}}